+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Deleting a category currently removes or invalidates products, carts, and orders that reference it, and can make the deleted category endpoint fail with a server error. Category deletion must be isolated to category records and associations so merchant catalog data and historical commerce remain usable.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Delete only the selected category, its descendants, and their product-category associations.
+- Preserve products, inventory, pricing, carts, and orders when their categories are deleted.
+- Return HTTP 404 for missing categories, deleted categories, and product listings filtered by deleted category.
+- Ensure deleted category associations are absent from product detail and category listings.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+- `category-deletion`: Safe deletion of category trees while preserving products and commerce references.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+## Impact
+
+- Category REST API and category facade/service deletion flow.
+- Product-category persistence mappings and product/category query behavior.
+- Integration tests covering category deletion, product detail, product filtering, carts, and orders.
